        "findings": [
          "The new full-limb noise helper assembles the same 66-byte domain-separated frame as the original hash function: prefix, LE16 tag length, noise tag, LE32 challenge/label/counter lengths, exact challenge and label, and LE32 counter. It computes a fresh whole-input SHA-256 per original checkpoint; this static comparison is not a speed result.",
          "Counter bound 128, callback-before-hash, same rejection test against Q, same LE32 extraction, partial final digest consumption and immediate cancellation are preserved in the reviewed source. The selected default FULL_LIMB path calls the new helper; retained reference paths still call the original helper. No hash-state, result or authority cache is introduced.",
          "Both selected project and local-closure pon_work pins must be updated; noise_frame must enter the actual six-crate Rust inventory. The existing reader enforces complete Rust inventory inside those crate roots and the eight literal includes, while still disclaiming Rust #[path] imports outside roots and external compiled dependency identity.",
          "The three mapping consumers (proof profile, upstream withdrawal and route registry), current reader literals, and independent current-reader tests need exact new hashes/counts. Updating these pins must not change the historical reader/contract, held upstream profile, empty approved_current_profile_ids, 15 unresolved obligations, null lifetime/security bounds or qualification booleans.",
          "The hash-use reader intentionally binds declared paths and 19 existing purposes and explicitly disclaims whole-callgraph/refinement coverage. Its proposed two-pin update may preserve those semantics and 31 declared paths, but cannot claim that inventory by itself now binds every newly introduced noise helper call. The separate current W1 closure is what adds that module pin.",
          "Two other manifests retain direct old pon_work pins: joint-consensus-qualification-v1 and w1-lifetime-current-source-v2. They are outside the three mapping-contract consumers. This review does not approve silently repinning them or claiming every current reader is closed."
        ],
